Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Prachi Nagar
Title: A Systematic Review of the Gender Gap in Digital Financial Inclusion in India Using PRISMA
Abstract: India has moved towards a near-universal bank account penetration, while the Unified Payments Interface (UPI) has enabled billions of transactions to take place each month. But the evidence indicates that the gender gap in financial inclusion has widened, from having an account to using one. Sixty-three records from the Scopus database were selected and a systematic review was performed using the PRISMA methodology. The results reveal that education, employment, income and digital access are always found to be important factors in explaining much of the difference, with a significant unaccountable factor remaining, indicating norms and control of accounts in the household. The review emphasizes the importance of usage-centred measurement and a gender-oriented design of digital payment systems.
