Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Soham Jain
Title: When Do Megawatts Become Alpha? A Conditional Transmission Framework Linking Renewable Energy Deployment to the Equity Returns of Renewable Energy Firms
Abstract: Global renewable power capacity is expected to almost double between 2025 and 2030, and many investors expect to earn higher equity returns from the physical expansion of the renewable energy industry. Clean-energy stocks, however, lost around 40% of their value between 2021 and the end of 2023, while renewables grew at a record pace. This paper examines whether renewable energy-related firms' stock prices in the U.S. reflect growth in renewable energy activity. The monthly return of the Nasdaq Clean Edge Green Energy Index (CELS) is regressed against the monthly change in the 10-year real Treasury yield, the monthly U.S. market excess return, and the monthly growth of U.S. renewable electricity generation. The findings suggest that growth in megawatts does not necessarily lead to returns for shareholders.
