Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Atiksh Sinha
Title: Bihar-Jharkhand Inclusion and Rights Guide
Abstract: Every child in India has rights on paper, but for many children from Scheduled Caste, Adivasi and other marginalised communities in Bihar and Jharkhand, those rights are hard to reach. This guide follows a life from birth to adulthood across five stages: early childhood, the school years, adolescence, entry into work, and adulthood and leadership. Each chapter opens with real-life scenarios of exclusion, explains the laws and schemes that protect people at that stage, identifies the gaps between rights on paper and rights in practice, and offers practical recommendations for schools, nonprofits, local authorities, companies, contractors and community groups.
