Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Pranav Narra
Title: Electricity Generation and the Energy Transition in Germany, and its Implications on the Globe
Abstract: The energy transition (Energiewende) in the German power sector has changed the sources of electricity production, yet comparatively little attention has been paid to the quantity of electricity produced. This study examines the correlations between Germany's total gross electricity generation and the generation mix and electricity prices. The data comprise 12 annual observations (2005 and 2015 to 2025). Total generation was negatively correlated with the renewables share (r = -0.750, p = .005) and positively correlated with the nuclear share (r = 0.751, p = .005) and the coal share (r = 0.764, p = .004). Neither the wholesale price nor the industrial price was significantly correlated with total generation.
